From 74256d3df55d2a0ce64274c2265c5c9b7022facb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 13:58:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] CMake: module for the sources containing kernels of MFEM

The function `mfem_mgis_compile_as_device_code` moves from
`FindMFEM.cmake` to the installed module `MFEMMGISDeviceCode.cmake`,
always loaded, also when a project finds MFEM before mfem-mgis. MFEM is
described by global properties set by `FindMFEM.cmake`, or by the
configuration file of mfem-mgis with the values used to build it.

- `mfem_mgis_enable_device_language()` enables CUDA when MFEM uses it.
  The CUDA compiler and its host compiler default to the ones of MFEM
  (`MFEM_CXX`, `MFEM_HOST_CXX`): the host compiler of MFEM finds the
  headers of MPI. CMake 3.18 is required in this case.
- GPU architectures read from all the forms of the options of nvcc
  (`-arch`, `--gpu-architecture`, `-gencode`, separate or joined values,
  `native`, `all`, `all-major`, `sm_XXa`); a warning when none is found,
  instead of an empty `CUDA_ARCHITECTURES`.
- Explicit errors when MFEM uses HIP (not supported yet) or when the CUDA
  language is not enabled.
- Options of nvcc only given to nvcc (not to clang in CUDA mode).
- C++ standard of the target (or of MFEM), shared CUDA runtime (as
  MFEM), definitions and visibility options of `CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS` given to
  the CUDA sources (`_GLIBCXX_DEBUG` changes the standard containers).
- `-isystem` directories quoted.
- Tests of the device and of the absolute tolerance of hypre out of the
  block requiring TFEL; option `enable-gpu-tests`; test of the GPU with
  two processes.
